x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits both the C1 and C2 constructor of Box<int> and Box<double> where clang emits only the C2 a use needs - the constructors are defined inline, and on this target clang emits the base-object form alone and calls it. The same difference move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames record; arm64-darwin and x86_64-windows agree on every name. cxx1's extra C1 is a mergeable superset and the case links and runs.
